# Review areas: which paths belong to which area, and who owns each area.
#
# Read by the review harness (and scripts/review-context.mjs), not by GitHub.
# GitHub only reads CODEOWNERS from .github/, the repo root, or docs/, so this
# file never auto-requests reviewers.
#
# Format: CODEOWNERS-style globs, relative to the repo root, grouped into
# sections. Globs also support {a,b} alternatives (picomatch syntax).
# A section header names the area and its owners:
#
#   [area-slug] @owner1 @owner2
#
# Every glob under a header belongs to that area, and the area's rubric is
# review/areas/<area-slug>.md. Unlike GitHub CODEOWNERS, every matching area
# applies, not just the last match. A colocated *.test.ts file belongs to the
# area of its sibling source file.
#
# Each area needs at least one owner. PRs that match no area go to two team
# members picked at random by scripts/review-context.mjs, from the people
# listed here who committed in the past week.
# TODO: request the Next.js oncall instead, once Vercel Agent supports it.

